data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 11, the EF Core Azure Cosmos DB provider **removes the sync-over-async opt-in entirely**. The synchronous LINQ operators (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()`, etc.) now throw `InvalidOperationException` unconditionally — there is no configuration to re-enable them.

In .NET 10 you could suppress this with:
```csharp
options.UseCosmos(...).ConfigureWarnings(w =>
    w.Ignore(CosmosEventId.SyncNotSupported));
```

That warning ID / suppression no longer exists in .NET 11.

## How to Fix

Convert to async throughout:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `Add()` remains synchronous (it only tracks in memory).
- All query execution and `SaveChanges` must be async.
- Callers must propagate `async/await` up the call stack ("async all the way").
